The USER GUIDE files are GUIDE0.VTH to GUIDE8.VTH, with the first file being   
the HELP MENU. These files--
All commands will accept upper or lower case letters, but the password must be 
entered in the same case(s) as used when initially set. On certain computer    
systems the operating system provides type-ahead buffering from the console    
keyboard, contain all ASCII characters, and can be printed if 
required. VIEWTEXT generates page and form files with extensions .PGE, .FRM and
.SPD for the page, form and speed page directories. These files contain binary 
information and cannot be displayed or printed other than by VIEWTEXT without  
unpredictable results.                                                         
                                                                               
In order to separate VIEWTEXT command files from dat the cable
and this port must be set up as described above.                               
                                                                               
PRINTER SETTING - the internal graphics mapping of VIEWTEXT is set for the OKI 
Ma files it is recommended  
that a new system disc be created, and all files on the VIEWTEXT master disc   
be moved to the new disc. If there is insufficient room, do not copy the HELP  
text files (any file with extension .VTH). These files can be lisICROLINE 80 series printers, and if the host system is equipped with this type
of printer the full PRESTEL graphics will be reproduced. The CONFIGURATION MENU
allows a flag to be set if using a MICROLINE or compatible printer to produce  
correct graphited instead.  
If the User Guide is called from the MAIN MENU the help files will be reported 
as missing from the disc, but no harm will be done.                            
