QUICK GUIDE - to run VIEWTEXT, select Dialling Directory (fu                               (C) TANDATA   1984
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SETTING THE BAUD RATE - the TANDATA Tm110 and Td 1400/Td 1600 Viewdata Adaptors
require a 1200 speed setting on the communinction 1 of the    
MAIN MENU) and prepare a directory entry with a telephone number, password and 
ID (see section 2 of the User Guide). Press ESCAPE twice to return to the      
dialling prompt, and press "L" to load the entry to the modem, followed bcations port used. The VIEWTEXT     
module does not set the baud rate, and therefore this must be done by the user 
with the correct local utility supplied with the host CP/M system. The format  
should be set to 1200 baud, 7 bits, even parity, 1 stop y the 
directory entry number, COMMA, and the modem directory number. When the entry  
has been loaded, press "D" to dial. The modem directory will be displayed on   
the left side of the screen. Enter the modem directory number (1-8) to select  
the dbit.                   
                                                                               
MODEM CABLE - the cable supplied with the VIEWTEXT system connects the modem to
an appropriate port on the computer system. The port is identified onialling information which has been loaded. The modem will dial the number,
and when connected will send out the password and the ID. Incoming pages will  
appear on the left side of the screen. To change screens, press CTRL and "P"   
together. Pages can be called by entering "*pagenumber!" or any digits or      
characters specified on the displayed page to select the next page choice. To  
return to the MAIN MENU, press ESCAPE twice. DISCONNECT (17) when finished.    
